# ══════════ Abstract ══════════
para("Abstract", bold=True, size=12, align=C, count=False)
para("Genre Dynamics and Policy Conjunctures in Jinjiang Literature City's Dual Markets: An Analysis of 3.86 Million Catalog Metadata Records (2003–2026)", bold=True, align=C, count=False)
para("Hohyun Lyu", align=C, count=False)
para("This study analyzes 3,856,274 catalog metadata records collected from Jinjiang Literature City (2003–2026) by decomposing the platform's catalog into two fully separated markets—original (原创) and derivative (衍生) works—and by cross-examining each major inflection point in the genre landscape against China's policy conjunctures. Five findings emerge. First, in the original market, romance (爱情) declined from its 2010 peak of 88.2% to 56.4% in 2024, with the drama genre (剧情) absorbing the decline, while wuxia was marginalized through elementization—trends the author's prior original-market analysis first identified, here re-verified through independent re-collection and extended to 2026. Second, the derivative market underwent a distinct restructuring: Chinese-source fanfiction (东方衍生) held 85–96% of the market from 2009 to 2017, then collapsed within two years—from 85.0% in 2017 to 30.6% in 2019—as fandom sources diversified toward Japanese ACGN and other global origins. Third, these inflections repeatedly synchronize with the policy timeline: the 2018–19 derivative restructuring coincides with the rectification campaign in which Jinjiang itself voluntarily closed two Chinese-setting (东方) sections and received suspension orders, and the drama genre's leap, which began amid the 2018–19 rectification phase, accelerated through the 227 incident, the Qinglang campaign, and the dan-gai prohibition. Rather than asserting causality, the study submits three mechanism hypotheses—classification/space intervention, creation-posting contraction, and detour into narrativity—each grounded in officially documented measures, press-confirmed platform actions, and fandom-studies accounts of tactical response. Fourth, title keywords form a dual convention system, standardizing metanarrative devices while absorbing internet buzzwords within a year of their emergence. Fifth, the creator base is a hyper-churn pool while reception concentrates in a superstar structure. Methodologically, the study empirically demonstrates that year-filter-based 'exhaustive' collection systematically omits undated serializing works (0.13% vs. 12.8–14.5% omission), measures the composition of the omitted stratum to show the study's core estimates are conservative lower bounds, and records the platform's 2026 access restriction as evidence that exhaustive observability is itself a historical condition.", count=False)
para("", count=False)
para("Key words : web novel, Jinjiang Literature City, genre dynamics, derivative work, fandom, content regulation, 227 incident, dan-gai, title keyword, creator turnover, superstar economy, data collection bias", count=False)

